  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-503001 Timewriting</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam (consortium lead) and CNV Internationaal (lead partner) have participated actively in the RSPO, focusing their efforts on promoting and strengthening the principles and criteria (P&lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;C), as well as the protocols and guidelines related to human rightsandcommunities involved with and often affected by palm oil operations, including workers, indigenous communities, women, and human rights defenders, as well as human rights organizations. The effective implementation of standards, policies, and protocols requires the active and qualified participation of these groups, who are familiar with these tools and know how to use them. Effective implementation also requires the RSPO and the companies auditing its standards to be familiar with the social movements, labor unions, and human rights organizations, to ask for their assessments in certifying or evaluating a company. In
this regard, the objectives of Oxfam and CNV Internationaal in their work in RSPO are very much aligned with the objectives of the RSPO outreach program, which seeksto ensure informed and qualified participation from communities and workers of the RSPO at all levels, establishing stronger linkages with the RSPO through intermediary organizations, and for civil society organizations (CSOs) and local governments to be aware ofthe RSPO and its mechanisms, facilitating active and informed community participation in the implementation of sustainability efforts by producers and palm oil companies.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib was founded in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Oxfam Novib is member of the Oxfam International confederation. Working together in the confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education for all, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam Novib&apos;s main office is based in The Netherlands, it supports the work of a network of local offices, the implementation of global projects, fundraising, campaigning and advocacy.  Oxfam Novib&#x92;s the Hague office contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
